  "location": "LEV30.3 second example",
  "text": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Basel Framework: LEV30.3 second example",
      "summary": "LEV30.3 cites CAP10.19 for the IRB provisions-shortfall deduction from CET1, but CAP10.19 covers the opposite case (excess provisions in Tier 2); the deduction is in CAP30.13.",
      "impact": "Position: IRB bank, EL 100, eligible provisions 70, shortfall 30 Reading a: follow CAP10.19 literally: no shortfall deduction found there, so no 30 'deducted from CET1' basis for LEV30.3 -> exposure measure not reduced by 30 Reading b: read as CAP30.13: 30 deducted from CET1, so 30 may be deducted from exposure measure Difference: exposure measure differs by 30",
      "correction": "Clarify or correct the cited passage so that the rule and its references give one result for the stated case."
    }
  },
